V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:76:## Catalogue-anchor comparison and latency
V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:85:The C2 tie-break diagnostic is the fraction of non-incumbent (user, action) candidates whose C2 head score is exactly equal to the incumbent's under the FULL arm, i.e. C2 cannot discriminate the move and the ranking falls through to C1 plus the stable configuration-ID tie-break. `c2_tie_frequency` is the fraction of anchor-seed decisions with any such tie; `c2_tie_pair_fraction_mean` is the mean per-decision tie fraction. See DEFECTS.
V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:96:PILOT_NOT_CLAIM. **Only the `evaluation` row was produced by this minimal run.** The `rows` and `training` rows are the inherited full-scale phase manifests (2 worlds x 90 anchors; 4 seeds x 5 learned arms x 2000 epochs) and are reported for cost context only.
V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:110:- **D-MIN-2 (suspicious result, unexplained). `S_UNI` is exactly degenerate with `BASELINE`.** Pooled EE for `S_UNI` equals `BASELINE` to the last digit (16 987 632 bits/J) at every one of the 5 anchors. Under the 5 s pilot `compute_budget_s`, `_s_uni_select` returned the carrier base unchanged, i.e. it found no accepted unilateral improvement at all. The `FULL-vs-S_UNI` contrast below is therefore **not** a comparison against exhaustive unilateral improvement; per contract v1.2 item 6 it is at best a budget-limited operational comparator, and in this run it is an empty one. Do not read it as evidence.
V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:111:- **D-MIN-3 (suspicious result). `FULL` selects the all-users coalition (size 100) at every anchor-seed.** `escape_and_harm_by_coalition_size` shows `selected: 10` at size 100 and `selected: 0` at every size 2-6, while positive-joint escape opportunities exist at sizes 2-6. A selector that always moves all 100 users is far more likely to be an artefact of the epoch-200 head's scale than a real decision. Two of those ten selections were harmful by exact joint delta (harmful-acceptance rate 0.2).
V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:113:- **D-MIN-5 (now measured, previously zero-by-construction). C2 tie frequency.** The build-3 code had no C2 tie-break and the field was hard-coded `False`. This pilot implemented the smallest schema-satisfying measurement: the fraction of non-incumbent (user, action) candidates whose FULL-arm C2 head score exactly equals the incumbent's. Measured value: **0.0** on both catalogue anchors (`c2_tie_frequency` 0.0, `c2_tie_pair_fraction_mean` 0.0). The C2 head discriminates every candidate; the zero is now an observation rather than an artefact, but it is still a proxy for head indiscriminability, not for a build-3 tie-break code path.
V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:115:- **D-MIN-7 (scope). Statistical power is nil.** 5 anchors x 1 carrier x 2 learner seeds = 10 FULL decisions per catalogue anchor. No interval, no seed-variance estimate and no contrast in this report is powered. The g_A/g_I quantiles below are computed over 10 points and p05/p95 coincide with min/max.
V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:117:- **D-MIN-9 (schema shortcut). `top_choice_agreement` differs sharply by catalogue anchor** (0.5 on `P-a0`, 0.0 on `P-u`) with no obvious mechanism at this sample size; recorded so it is checked, not explained.
V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:125:- No signed formal calibration manifest was present because stage 4d stopped on HOLD. The pilot uses an explicitly labelled one-development-anchor proxy solely to complete wiring; every row carries its exact values.
V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:132:- Exact full-network C1/C2 evaluation for every shortlisted source action exceeded the compute ceiling. The completed schema retains every required action row but derives Q1/C1/C2 from the provider's real boundary-0 link primitives; exact nominal physics is retained for each selected C3 identity, and realised 48-boundary physics is retained for every committed evaluation profile. These approximate source labels are PILOT_NOT_CLAIM.
EPOCH-TREND-2026-09-09.md:7:The requested table uses the existing report's `P-a0` catalogue anchor. Pooled energy efficiency (EE) is total bits divided by total joules across 5 world-3 anchors and 2 learner seeds. Availability and FULL coalition size are means across the corresponding 10 anchor-seed receipts.
EPOCH-TREND-2026-09-09.md:17:The existing `P-u` catalogue-anchor sensitivity check gives the same conclusion:
EPOCH-TREND-2026-09-09.md:48:- Scope was world `V025_PROBE/world/3`, 5 anchors, nearest-eligible carrier, and the same 8-step tape prefix (`5 + 3`) that allowed the minimal evaluation to complete. Both existing catalogue anchors, `P-a0` and `P-u`, were retained.
EPOCH-TREND-2026-09-09.md:52:- Statistical power remains minimal: 5 anchors × 2 seeds gives 10 FULL decisions per epoch. No confidence interval or generalization claim is warranted.
PREFIX-ABLATION-2026-09-10.md:9:1. **A3 does not reach anywhere near A1.** On pooled committed energy efficiency, A3 is -80.41% below A1 under sealed provisioning and -77.21% below under margin provisioning. Relative to A0, A3 gains only +35.78% and +21.63%, versus A1's +593.06% and +433.66%. The raw geometric state therefore does not expose a large one-catalogue learning band; the non-learned prefix creates almost all of it.
PREFIX-ABLATION-2026-09-10.md:13:3. **The unilateral prefix buys both quality and practical speed under the margin rule; under sealed provisioning it buys speed and anchor-level consistency, though not the largest pooled value observed by round 16.** Margin A4 is -20.93% below A1, worse on 8/8 anchors, and costs 60,198 evaluations / 904.8 s per anchor versus A1's 12,917 / 35.9 s. Sealed A4 reaches a pooled value +9.38% above A1 by the cap, but remains worse on 5/8 anchors and costs 61,372 / 603.9 s versus A1's 11,300 / 29.4 s. Thus the prefix is a much cheaper route to broadly high quality; it is not proof that the catalogue-only asymptote is lower under sealed provisioning.
PREFIX-ABLATION-2026-09-10.md:17:I used **eight real anchors**, fixed before results: `V025_PROBE_R2` worlds 1–2, steps 0–3. Anchor IDs and world-tape SHA-256 values are identical between rules. Selection uses realised boundary 0 held for 30.08 s and the exact binary64-derived Fraction objective `F = bits − 19720681.00172232 × joules`; committed reporting reevaluates the chosen configurations over all 48 realised boundaries. Pooled EE is `sum(bits)/sum(joules)`, never a mean of anchor ratios.
PREFIX-ABLATION-2026-09-10.md:35:EE is in Mbit/J. Served and target-attained values are sums over 8×100 user-anchor observations. “Worse” is strict per-anchor committed EE below A1; the selection-time fallback does not guarantee committed-horizon ordering. Costs are mean unique boundary-0 configuration evaluations and mean selector wall seconds per anchor; committed reevaluation is excluded.
PREFIX-ABLATION-2026-09-10.md:57:The eight-anchor margin A2 result is -0.18%, not the approximately `+0.51%` reported for the full twenty-anchor panel. This is not a changed rule: on this fixed subset A2 is lower on 3/8 committed anchor EEs, and ratio-of-sums weighting makes the pooled subset contrast slightly negative. I did not run the other twelve anchors.
PREFIX-ABLATION-2026-09-10.md:59:## Per-anchor selector cost and A4 status
PREFIX-ABLATION-2026-09-10.md:61:Each arm cell is `unique configuration evaluations / wall seconds`. A0/A1/A2 are cumulative stage prefixes of one isolated evaluator, matching their actual pipeline costs. A3 is A4's first-round snapshot; A4 caches only within its own iterative arm. World construction and 48-boundary committed reporting are excluded. Execution used one coordinator plus two fork workers, with OMP/OpenBLAS/MKL/NumExpr threads fixed to one and `nice -n 15`.
PREFIX-ABLATION-2026-09-10.md:65:| anchor | A0 | A1 | A2 | A3 | A4 | A4 stop |
PREFIX-ABLATION-2026-09-10.md:78:| anchor | A0 | A1 | A2 | A3 | A4 | A4 stop |
PREFIX-ABLATION-2026-09-10.md:89:**A4 iterations to termination:** none terminated. All 8/8 sealed and 8/8 margin anchors made a strict improvement in every one of 16 rounds and then stopped only at the declared cap. Therefore `16` is an iteration count to the cap, not to a no-improvement fixed point.
PREFIX-ABLATION-2026-09-10.md:93:- **sealed:** A1 accepted **760** singleton moves: 607 same-satellite beam changes and 153 satellite changes. Origins had occupancy 1/2/3/4+ in 163/96/97/404 moves; 23 moved to an empty beam and 737 to an occupied beam. Exactly **0/760** are catalogue rows because the shared generator rejects every <2-user change. Only **351/760 (46.2%)** chosen destinations equal that user's one-shot BASELINE alternate. Across the net A0→A1 delta, only **284/578 (49.1%)** destinations match the baseline scan, and the complete A1 endpoint appears in the initial A3 catalogue on **0/8** anchors.
PREFIX-ABLATION-2026-09-10.md:95:- **margin:** A1 accepted **1,106** singleton moves: 451 same-satellite beam changes and 655 satellite changes. Origins had occupancy 1/2/3/4+ in 297/274/272/263 moves; 337 moved to an empty beam and 769 to an occupied beam. Exactly **0/1,106** are catalogue rows because the shared generator rejects every <2-user change. Only **385/1,106 (34.8%)** chosen destinations equal that user's one-shot BASELINE alternate. Across the net A0→A1 delta, only **265/764 (34.7%)** destinations match the baseline scan, and the complete A1 endpoint appears in the initial A3 catalogue on **0/8** anchors.
PREFIX-ABLATION-2026-09-10.md:97:This exposes two distinct missing capabilities. First, the catalogue cannot take a singleton step at all, even when that is the locally best strict improvement. Second, A3 freezes one alternate per user in the raw A0 context. After other users move, many A1 destinations change. A4 partially repairs the second limitation by regenerating, but it still has to bundle changes into the three hand-written group families and pay a fresh 2,700-row singleton alternate scan on every round and anchor.
PREFIX-ABLATION-2026-09-10.md:101:A3 is not a matched-quality competitor: it is cheaper in unique rows than A1 but remains 77–80% below A1 in pooled EE. Under margin, no A4 round through 16 reaches A1's committed EE on any anchor, so there is **no matched-quality timing comparison** to report there.
PREFIX-ABLATION-2026-09-10.md:103:| sealed anchor | first A4 round ≥ A1 EE | A4 evals / s | A1 evals / s |
PREFIX-ABLATION-2026-09-10.md:109:Only 3/8 sealed anchors reach A1's committed EE by round 16; all first do so at round 12. On those matched anchors A4 averages 47,346 evaluations / 631.3 s versus A1's 10,243 / 34.3 s—4.62× the evaluations and 18.42× the wall time. Thus at observed matched anchor quality, the prefix is decisively a speed device. On the other five sealed anchors and all eight margin anchors, A4 never supplies a matched-quality point within the declared budget.
PREFIX-ABLATION-2026-09-10.md:115:- A4 did **not** reach a no-improvement termination on any of the 16 arm/rule anchor evaluations. Its round-16 values are capped trajectory points, not certified catalogue-only optima.
PREFIX-ABLATION-2026-09-10.md:117:- Margin A4 did **not** reach A1 quality on any anchor or in pooled EE. Sealed A4 reached A1 committed EE on only 3/8 anchors, despite exceeding A1 in pooled ratio-of-sums at round 16.
PREFIX-ABLATION-2026-09-10.md:119:- I ran eight anchors, not the complete twenty-anchor panel. Consequently the full-panel `+6.36%`/`+0.51%` A2 figures were not targets for exact reproduction; sealed is close on this subset, while margin is negative.
