.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-controller-handoff-20260907/ADJUDICATION-PHYSICS-EE-ROUND4-RATE-TARGET-CODEX-GPT6-ASTRA-ULTRA-2026-09-08.md:16:- **Coherent default:** invert the actual ACM curve, \(\Gamma_r(n)=\min\{\gamma_m:WSE_m/n\ge r_*\}\), and count achieved decodable bits. Discrete modes produce overshoot; nominal control does not guarantee realized attainment. The raw Shannon inverse cannot be combined with the sealed ACM table and called exact rate delivery. [ETSI Table 13](https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/302300_302399/30230701/01.04.01_60/en_30230701v010401p.pdf), [profile conversion](/home/sat/mcrl-v023-astra-physics/astra-physics-round3-final.md:78)
.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-controller-handoff-20260907/ADJUDICATION-PHYSICS-EE-ROUND4-RATE-TARGET-CODEX-GPT6-ASTRA-ULTRA-2026-09-08.md:17:- **Floor + surplus ACM option:** a separately declared surplus-power rule, e.g. \(p=\min(p_{\max},p_{\rm required}+p_{\rm surplus})\), can preserve geometry→extra bits alongside power savings. Merely calling the target a “floor” does not; transmitting every slot at the cap removes angle→watts.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-controller-handoff-20260907/ADJUDICATION-PHYSICS-EE-ROUND4-RATE-TARGET-CODEX-GPT6-ASTRA-ULTRA-2026-09-08.md:18:- **Finite-demand option:** \(B_u=\min(d_u,\int R_u\,dt)\). C1 retains energy savings and delivery-shortfall reductions, C2 forecasts future power/availability, and C3 trades consolidation savings against congestion and cap failures. Demand clipping alone creates no energy mechanism; rate inversion or explicit duty control must supply it. [Demand/L1 distinction](/home/sat/mcrl-v023-codex-astra/trackb-next-lever-final.md:17)
.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-controller-handoff-20260907/ADJUDICATION-PHYSICS-EE-ROUND4-RATE-TARGET-CODEX-GPT6-ASTRA-ULTRA-2026-09-08.md:20:**C. Recommendation before outcomes.** Make **a-r primary**: it supplies the missing occupancy→required-power channel while preserving angle→power. Goal 2 requires C1’s positive EE contribution, not preservation of its original surplus-bits mechanism. Seal **50 Mbit/s**, explicitly a synthetic operating point—not calibrated demand. [Provenance](/home/sat/mcrl-v023-codex-astra/trackb-next-lever-final.md:31)
.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-controller-handoff-20260907/ADJUDICATION-PHYSICS-EE-ROUND4-RATE-TARGET-CODEX-GPT6-ASTRA-ULTRA-2026-09-08.md:29:> **Components:** regenerate C1’s whole-network surplus and C2’s future power/cap/service forecasts. C3 scores whole configurations and includes coordinated load transfers/swaps alongside evacuations, using one prospectively frozen catalogue across matched arms.  
.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-controller-handoff-20260907/ADJUDICATION-PHYSICS-EE-ROUND4-RATE-TARGET-CODEX-GPT6-ASTRA-ULTRA-2026-09-08.md:36:- Old finite-demand C3 marginals were −1.3866/−0.7524/0% at 200/50/10 Mbit/s, but retained old power and an **others-bits** C3 target. Those negatives remain valid historical findings; they do not test successor energy coordination. Reusing that target would make C3 vanish wherever exact rate delivery equalizes everyone’s bits. [Results](/home/sat/mcrl-v023-codex-astra/trackb-next-lever-final.md:3), [executed target](/home/sat/mcrl-v023-astra-c3core/15-ORACLE-MARGINALS-CODE/oracle_marginals.py:116)
